      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{62b61f8ec938a62475e4cd14|full_name} I tried the perf-test branch and it doesn't have the problem.\n\nIn the current stable build, the cpu and gpu usage is considerably higher when looking at a mirror and the frames are reduced heavily.\n\nThis problem isn't seen in perf-test, it has lower cpu and gpu usage with much higher frames like previous stable builds had.\n\nI don't know if it's specifically related to mirrors, but that's where I'm seeing the most obvious difference.\n\nEdit: Just wanted to add that the regression I'm seeing is still present in the latest stable build 1819 that was just pushed out recently.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
